{"name":"Old Salem","hex":"#bba582","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"}],"entries":[{"title":"Old Salem","blocks":[{"text":"Old Salem is a historic district of Winston-Salem, North Carolina, United States, which was originally settled by the Moravian community in 1766. It features a living-history museum which interprets the restored Moravian community. The non-profit organization began its work in 1950, although some private residents had restored buildings earlier. As the Old Salem Historic District, it was declared a National Historic Landmark (NHL) in 1966, and expanded fifty years later. The district showcases the culture of the Moravian settlement in the Province of North Carolina during the colonial 18th century and post-statehood 19th century via its communal buildings, churches, houses and shops."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Old_Salem-1.jpg/330px-Old_Salem-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Salem","wikidata":"Q844445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Home_Moravian_Church.jpg/500px-Home_Moravian_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Home_Moravian_Church.jpg/500px-Home_Moravian_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Home Moravian Church, 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHome_Moravian_Church.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/